Subject: [PATCH] webrtc: answer the given address after a round trip through the proxy

The server-reflexive candidate gathered for --fingerprint-webrtc-ip came
20 to 60 ms after the binding request. A host at the proxy's address
cannot hear from a STUN server sooner than a round trip through the
proxy, and WHOX measured the answer faster than its own TCP round trip
to that address.

The renderer now passes the allocator the longest round trip the browser
already timed for the frame and its ancestor documents in its process:
the TLS handshake of each connection their document and subresource
loads opened through the proxy, which is one round trip to that server
with no server time in it. A detector's STUN server is one of the page's
servers or nearer. Without a handshake, the document's wait for its
response headers counts. The synthetic STUN answer comes after that
round trip, capped at a second, plus up to a sixteenth of it as jitter;
without any timed load, after 90 to 160 ms. Candidates keep their order
and gathering still completes after the server-reflexive candidate.
Nothing new is sent: no UDP leaves the machine and no request is made to
time the proxy.

